WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.600
I'm going to try something today that's very
important and will certainly be useful, but

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.649
I don't know how much people, people

00:00:06.649 --> 00:00:11.540
will be entertained by it, which is that I'm
going to go through some of the propaganda

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.129
that we've been hearing from Republicans who
defend Donald Trump and are of course against

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:20.460
his impeachment conviction in the current
Senate impeachment trial.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.580
And bear with me because I do think this is
going to shed a ton of light on what we've

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.580
been seeing.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.420
And it's also going to show you how the pro
Trump right is developing their strategy around

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.089
disconfirming the public on the impeachment
of Donald Trump.

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:37.850
And what we saw during the Senate impeachment
trial is that during the breaks, when they

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:43.600
have these 15 to 45 minute breaks in the proceeding,
senators and members of the house will sometimes

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.139
talk to the press and basically the term Gish
Gallop is representative of what we've been

00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:54.719
seeing in the Senate trial, uh, from Donald
Trump's lawyers and also outside of it from

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:56.179
Republican lawmakers.

00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:57.739
During these little press avails.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:04.339
Gish Gallop is defined as a technique used
during debate that focuses on overwhelming

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:09.729
an opponent with as many arguments as possible
without regard for the accuracy or the strength

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:10.799
of those arguments.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:16.170
So during the presentations by Donald Trump's
lawyers over the last couple of days, the

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:21.240
attorneys will get up there and they'll say
there was no pressure on the Ukrainian president

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.369
because he said there was no pressure.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:27.700
But anyway, the military aid was released
and abusive power isn't an impeachable offense

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.090
and there's no crime.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:34.670
And Adam Schiff won't testify and they had
secret basement meetings and we have no firsthand

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:35.670
testimony.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.890
And back in 1996 when bill Clinton was being
impeached, Jerry Nadler said this thing or

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.259
that thing or whatever the case may be, it's
so much, and the way that it's supposed to

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:50.619
work on you and it is working on a lot of
people, is that you say, wow, that's a lot.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:51.829
I guess they're right.

00:01:51.829 --> 00:01:55.960
I don't know how those things are related
because they're not, of course, I don't know

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.759
how those things relate to the impeachment
of Donald Trump because they don't, but it

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:02.360
sounds overwhelming.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.360
That's a lot of stuff.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:08.200
I guess Donald Trump isn't guilty of any kind
of wrongdoing and this has been a huge challenge

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:14.280
to us in covering the Senate trial live because
it's impossible to go point by point without

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.310
then missing a ton of stuff that they continue
to say.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.140
So let's try just one of these in detail.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.930
We'll go through what was said.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.300
This example is Congresswoman Elise Stefanik.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.850
She's a Republican from New York.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.430
During one of these breaks in the proceedings
yesterday, a reporter asks a question and

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:36.030
she jumps in with some Gish Gallop and note
that Donald Trump retweeted this video of

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.440
Elise Stefanik.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.180
He loves it, but it's just nonsense.

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.180
Take a look at the clip.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:42.180
Do you run?

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.180
You need the 10 sky.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.120
This security assistance to pressure Ukraine
to investigate, but that's okay.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.460
He did not because the aid was released to
Ukraine and there was no investigation and

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.330
the president, the president has said that
he did not tie.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.710
There was no conditionality or an insomnia
and in fact testified and we saw that played

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:03.220
out as the president's defense team made the
case that it was presumption, assumption and

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.220
guesswork.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:08.600
So the facts of this case remain the same
in that we have more security assistance for

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.900
Ukraine, much more than during the Obama administration.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.940
And there was in fact no investigation into
the Bidens but the administration, the administration

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:16.940
has to lose it.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.510
This was Adam shovel choice, Adam, Adam Schiff,
Adam Schiff, Adam Schiff is clearly scared

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.270
that his case is so weak.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.030
Adam Schiff made the decision to withdraw
the subpoena.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:31.210
This is an unfair unconstitutional and half
baked set of impeachment articles that was

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.520
sent over to the Senate [inaudible].

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.520
So

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.180
that's a ton of stuff and it sounds so open
and shut.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.610
It sounds so overwhelming.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.340
How could she possibly be wrong about what
she's saying?

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.240
But let's break it down with the transcript
on the screen.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:51.690
The reporter asks if the president did tie
the security assistance to pressure Ukraine

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.980
to investigate Biden.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:04:00.700
That's okay, so she mentions that the aid
was released, but the thing is it was eventually

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:04.630
released because this became a scandal and
they realized it.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:08.470
So yes, they release the aid, but that's not
exculpatory.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.130
She says the aid was released to say that's
exculpatory.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.910
They release the aid because they got caught
and they said, we better release this aid

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.500
because it's starting to look really, really
bad.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.140
Then she says, Trump said there was no conditionality.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.730
Well, that's what's being debated here.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.760
Her saying there was no conditionality doesn't
make it true.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.230
Her saying Trump's opinion is there was no
conditionality also doesn't make it true.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:38.030
She's asserting an opinion as a fact after
saying something that is not actually exculpatory.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:44.720
She then says, Gordon Sunderland testified
and Trump's defense team says it was presumption,

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.030
assumption and guesswork.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.140
Remember, that is not a fact.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:55.180
She says the people being paid to defend Donald
Trump, his lawyers are attacking Gordon Sunderland's

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.660
testimony is merely speculative.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:03.000
If you go and look at Sunderland's testimony,
he says very clearly there was a quid pro

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.890
quo with regard to the announcement of investigating
Joe Biden and I infer that there was likely

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:13.700
one for military aid, although he can't say
for sure you can disagree with Sunland.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:19.340
You can think Sundland is wrong, that he's
mistaken, that he's lying even, but she States

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.240
the argument of Trump's lawyers as fact.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.980
There is a debate about that.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.630
She throws it into the Gish Gallop as fact.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.260
Then she says, we now have more assistance
from Ukraine than under the Obama administration.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.760
Again, that is not evidence for or against
wrongdoing when it comes to the impeachment

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.760
articles.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:42.350
The total aid amounts to different countries
go up and down for a bunch of different reasons.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:43.350
Over time.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.030
It is a non-sequitur.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:49.889
She then says there didn't end up being an
investigation into the Bidens.

00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:51.350
This is both irrelevant.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:56.550
If you fail to secure the smear investigation
you wanted, you're not less guilty, you just

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.550
failed.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:02.910
But more importantly, witnesses have said,
Trump didn't care about the investigation

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.000
happening.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.570
He only cared about the investigation being
announced.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:12.470
So saying there was no investigation that
is not exculpatory.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.590
Okay.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.340
Then she switches altogether and this is where
it really escalates.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:23.250
After being asked about the John Bolton subpoena,
she says, Adam Schiff is scared.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.169
That's not an assertion of any kind of actual
fact that's been presented.

00:06:27.169 --> 00:06:29.090
She's using it as an ad hominem.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.660
She's alleging fear as an ad hominem, and
then she says, shift decided not to subpoena

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.430
John Bolton implying that the testimony of
John Bolton wouldn't help shift.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.940
And that's why shift decided not to issue
the subpoena.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:45.320
Now, in reality, they didn't subpoena John
Bolton because due to the obstruction of the

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:51.340
white house, it could take a year for the
forcing of that subpoena to go through the

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.550
judiciary.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:55.280
And by then it would be after the November
election and this entire thing would have

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.280
gone nowhere.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.669
It's not evidenced one way or the other about
Donald Trump's guilt that Adam Schiff decided

00:07:00.669 --> 00:07:03.250
not to issue a subpoena for John Bolton.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:10.080
And then again, a non-sequitur she goes to,
this is an unfair, unconstitutional impeachment.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.480
That is not true.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:16.490
Whether it's unfair, Senate Republicans can
vote and it's certainly not unconstitutional.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.150
So notice how it started with a question.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:24.199
Would it be okay for Donald Trump to tie military
aid to Ukraine to an investigation of Joe

00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:25.440
Biden?

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.290
She Gish gallops herself all the way to the
entire thing is unconstitutional.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:36.030
If you just casually watch those 53 seconds
of Elise Stefanik without really thinking

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:41.040
through each piece, it does sound like, wow,
that's an overwhelming amount of stuff that

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:45.340
she said Trump must be innocent because look
at all those things that she said.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:48.800
When you break it down, there is no substance
to what she says.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:55.210
It's conjecture, speculation, mischaracterizations
and complete misdirection to irrelevant.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.260
Nonsequitors.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:08:01.070
We could do that with almost any clip of these
Republicans talking to the press during the

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:02.070
breaks.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.070
This is just one clip.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.470
Imagine what there would be if you looked
at others.

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:06.700
Let's do one more briefly.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:11.850
We won't do it in as much detail because this
relates to witnesses in the trial.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:17.070
The new line from Republicans about bringing
in witnesses like John Bolton is we'll decide

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:22.620
whether we need to hear more after the trial
is basically done, and this is actually evil.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:27.040
Genius Republicans have done something insane
to begin with, which is they decided at the

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.270
beginning.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:33.610
We won't decide now about about witnesses
to impeachment or documents or audio visual

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.559
records in a normal trial.

00:08:36.559 --> 00:08:42.199
At the start of the trial, it's determined
who is on your witness list, what evidence

00:08:42.199 --> 00:08:47.670
do you plan to introduce and then both sides
get to prepare their case on the basis of

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.379
who's going to be testifying.

00:08:49.379 --> 00:08:55.750
Republicans successfully pushed off debating
witnesses until after each side gets 24 hours

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.369
to present and senators get 16 hours to ask
questions.

00:09:00.369 --> 00:09:02.399
So now they're using this line.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:04.610
Listen to Republican Senator John Barrasso
here

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:09.890
cause we're going to decide Friday on witnesses,
but it's not going to be a one-sided issue.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:10.890
We have another day.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:14.339
We have this evening tomorrow for the president's
case to be presented.

00:09:14.339 --> 00:09:18.910
We have 16 hours of questioning on Thursday,
Wednesday and Thursday.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.960
And then ultimately with the question will
come, have we heard enough?

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:28.160
Are we ready to go to final judgment or do
we need to hear from more people?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:33.059
If we need to hear from more people, it's
going to be a group of individuals, but 51

00:09:33.059 --> 00:09:36.589
senators will make that decision on Friday
and not before Friday.

00:09:36.589 --> 00:09:37.589
He's

00:09:37.589 --> 00:09:39.730
saying, listen, we've had all this questioning,
right?

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.120
We're, we're, we've done so much.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.970
We're going to do 24 hours for the managing
impeachment managers.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.240
24 hours for Trump's defense, 16 hours of
questions.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.029
That's 64 hours.

00:09:49.029 --> 00:09:53.119
After 64 hours, we'll decide whether we've
heard enough or whether we need to hear from

00:09:53.119 --> 00:09:54.339
more people.

00:09:54.339 --> 00:09:58.699
This is a completely different framing now
before the trial, which is when they should

00:09:58.699 --> 00:10:03.140
discuss witnesses, uh, you can't use the argument
they're now using.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.459
We have a trial.

00:10:04.459 --> 00:10:05.620
Who are the witnesses?

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:09.779
Well, you're going to decide based on whether
you want to hear more.

00:10:09.779 --> 00:10:13.639
They are going to say 64 hours is a long time.

00:10:13.639 --> 00:10:16.069
We've had presentations, we've had questions.

00:10:16.069 --> 00:10:18.360
We don't really need more stuff now.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:24.350
It's already gone on too long because they
blocked the decision about witnesses from

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.370
the start.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.689
It's incredibly disingenuous.

00:10:27.689 --> 00:10:33.509
It's completely propagandistic and I hope
that this is useful to people in the audience

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:39.209
